<article class="env-definition" id="0E2T">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E2T">Definition <span data-tag="0E2T">48.28.1</span>.</a> Let $X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes which is flat and locally of finite presentation. Let $W \subset X \times _ S X$ be any open such that the diagonal $\Delta _{X/S} : X \to X \times _ S X$ factors through a closed immersion $\Delta : X \to W$. A <em>relative dualizing complex</em> is a pair $(K, \xi )$ consisting of an object $K \in D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ and a map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xi : \Delta _*\mathcal{O}_ X \longrightarrow L\text{pr}_1^*K|_ W  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(\mathcal{O}_ W)$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$K$ is $S$-perfect (Derived Categories of Schemes, Definition <a href="/tag/0DI0" data-tag="0DI0">36.35.1</a>), and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\xi $ defines an isomorphism of $\Delta _*\mathcal{O}_ X$ with $R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ W}( \Delta _*\mathcal{O}_ X, L\text{pr}_1^*K|_ W)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>